        "original_id": "bec2617b-b616-5cc3-9ad0-e378843a6709",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Sing Out for Ireland\n- Organizations: The Wolfe Tones\n- People: Theobald Wolfe Tone\n- Events: Irish Rebellion of 1798\n- Concepts: wolf tone\n\nFacts:\n- Theobald Wolfe Tone was one of the leaders of the Irish Rebellion of 1798.\n- The Wolfe Tones are an Irish folk and rebel band.\n- The Wolfe Tones take their name from Theobald Wolfe Tone.\n- The name The Wolfe Tones also refers to the double entendre of a wolf tone, a spurious sound that can affect instruments of the violin family.\n- Sing Out for Ireland is the fourteenth album by The Wolfe Tones.",
